## Why This Is Asked
This question exams diagnosing subtle cross-region telemetry issues tied to time synchronization, control-plane stability, MTU handling, and NIC behavior, not just data-path faults.

## Key Concepts
- Time synchronization protocols (NTP/PTP)
- EVPN route convergence and BFD timers
- UDP telemetry MTU/fragmentation implications
- NIC offloads and timestamp behavior

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: quick log parser for interval spikes
const fs=require('fs');
const lines=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[2],'utf8').split('\n');
let spikes=0;
lines.forEach(l=>{ if(/telemetry.*tail/.test(l)) spikes++;});
console.log('spikes',spikes);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate this diagnostic with a runbook?
- What thresholds would trigger configuration changes (timers, MTU, pacing)?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical DNS troubleshooting skills, anycast path reasoning, and ability to design a reproducible diagnostic plan with concrete commands.

## Key Concepts

- DNS resolution and TTL behavior
- Anycast routing and cache effects
- Health checks and traffic steering
- Reproducibility and data collection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: parse a dns trace to extract served A record
function extractRegion(traceLines) {
  const line = traceLines.find(l => l.includes('A')) || traceLines[0];
  const match = line.match(/([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}/);
  return match ? match[0] : null;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate a rollback plan if regional DNS changes cause regression?
- Which metrics signal a successful stabilization?
